course: dictionary
lesson: 1733
title: Claim: say it, ask for it, prove it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Claim» has several meanings, and the words around it show you which one fits. In «...though stories claim far more», claim means someone says something is true, even though it may not be proven.
explain: Claim can also mean asking for something that belongs to you. At the airport you go to baggage claim to collect your bags. The clue is that the bags are yours, so you are asking for them back.
explain: In science and debates, a claim is an idea that needs evidence to prove it. «A claim is true or false all by itself: two plus two is four whether a professor says it, a six-year-old says it, or your most annoying cousin says it.» Who says a claim does not change whether it is true. Always ask: what is the evidence?
fact: «Claim» can mean to say something is true, even when it is not proven.
fact: «Claim» can mean to ask for something because it belongs to you, like your prize or your luggage.
fact: A claim is also a statement that something is true, and in school it needs evidence to support it.
fact: An insurance claim is a request for money you are owed.
fact: «Claim to fame» means something you are well known for.
exercise: «The reticulated python is the longest snake, though stories claim far more.» In this sentence, what does claim mean? | *To say something is true, even though it may not be proven | To cook food slowly | To cause something to be lost | To ask for something that belongs to you
exercise: At the airport you go to baggage claim to get your bags. In this phrase, what does claim mean? | *To ask for something that belongs to you | To take a life | A rude remark | To say something is true
exercise: In a science lesson, your teacher says every claim needs evidence. What is a claim here? | A kind of snake | A prize you have won | A bag at the airport | *A statement that something is true
test: An insurance claim is a request for what? | A kind of song | A bird that lives on the sea | A long, slow walk | *Money you are owed
test: According to the lesson, what decides whether a claim is true or false? | How many people believe it | How old the speaker is | How loudly it is said | *Whether the claim itself is right, not who says it
exam: In «The fire claimed three houses», what does claimed mean? | To cook quickly | To say something is true | *To cause something to be lost | To ask for a prize
